{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The agent asks only for outgoing edges and submits without reading\n contents. Its renderer is required by the agent interface, but any\n rendering would imply an unwanted content input. Other agent tests\n exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]` is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Placement and form:** It sits on an explicit function with a body, and its explanation is in fenced citation commentary. That is the form `habeas:coverage` allows.\n- **Substantive reason:** The `render` body is `panic!(\"edge-only conversation must not render contents\")`. The function exists only because `AgentInputRenderer` is required by `ToolAgent::new` and `Validator::with_agent`. The test is a guard. It must never read or render node contents, and a panic here would fail it. That is a real reason the function stays unexecuted, not just difficulty.\n- **Agreement with source:** The renderer is called only from `GraphSession`'s `Conversation` `dispatch` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs`, and from `Ask::execute` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs`. In `dispatch` it renders a node's contents snapshot, which a content-read tool call reaches. The test's scripted agent calls only `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`. Its `node_content` and `fingerprint` also panic, and its asserted dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` only. So the claim that the agent asks only for outgoing edges and never renders contents matches the code.\n- **Other tests:** The commentary says other agent tests exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents. That is consistent with `render` being called only on a content-read path. I did not read those other tests.\n\nThe citation is a `cite` as the built-in requires. It is not redundant with any `impl` or `test` on this item.",
